    "narrative": "The Austin Waves look primed for a high-ceiling performance today, headlined by **Gunnar Henderson**, whose 83.29 score makes him our premier asset. **Gunnar Henderson** benefits significantly from a favorable park factor (+16%) and a strong platoon advantage against Melton, keeping him as the essential anchor for our 5x5 production. Following him, **Kyle Tucker** (70.33) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (67.94) provide steady, elite-tier reliability. While **Kyle Tucker** maintains a solid baseline, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** is positioned for a productive outing against Keller, bolstered by a strong 0.378 xwOBA which helps mitigate the slight drag from his platoon splits.\n\nThe most notable tactical decision today involved **Nasim Nunez**, who narrowly edged out bench options to maintain his utility spot. Despite batting eighth, **Nasim Nunez** benefits from a +11% boost due to the matchup against P\u00e9rez and his switch-hitting flexibility, providing a unique speed upside that we cannot afford to bench in such a scarce category. While **Jackson Merrill** (61.40) and **Andy Pages** (58.91) remain strong starts, we are keeping a close eye on **Liam Hicks** (53.47). His projection is heavily buoyed by an order-leading role today, though he remains a marginal play compared to our core stars. Meanwhile, our bench remains depleted by the injuries to **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Jordan Westburg**, and **Jacob Wilson**, leaving us with limited flexibility to rotate in reserves like **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, who is currently out of the lineup. Owners should monitor weather conditions closely, as any shift could further compress the value of our middle-of-the-pack starters like **Brayan Rocchio** (47.06) and **Miguel Vargas** (54.92), who rely heavily on these matchup projections to maintain their utility.",
